      "name": "maxHeight",
      "type": "Dp?",
      "required": false,
      "defaultValue": "null",
      "description": "Explicit viewport height cap for the panel, independent of size. `null` → derive the cap from size (S = 50, M = 70, L = 85, FullWidth = 100 percent of viewport height). When set: - content shorter than maxHeight → panel wraps its content (small window), - content taller → panel is capped at maxHeight and the body scrolls while header and footer stay fixed. Clamped to the available viewport (screen height − vertical window margins); a value larger than the viewport behaves as full height. size still drives width."
    },
